W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1 — HONEST-STOP per-knob ablation
======================================================

Date: 2026-05-24
Parent commit: e9054b53 (W44-PHASE4-S2-validate)
Status: RULED OUT — k2 is not the catastrophe driver
Production source: REVERTED to S2-refit raw optima (no change shipped)

Hypothesis
----------

W44-PHASE4-S2-validate (`e9054b53`) caught a W44-228c1 violation on the
opt-in Tier2Knobs path: terminal e8 d=4 dropped from 42,322 B / SSIM2
86.91 (Mode A, defaults) to 28,185 B / SSIM2 81.98 (Mode B,
auto_for_distance — the W44-PHASE4-S2-refit lookup applied).

The task spec proposed flooring screen/very_high
`screenshot_quant_aggressiveness` (k2) at 0.333 (matching the other 3
screen strata's value) to restore the W44-105 buttloop screen-seed
lift on terminal/imac_g3/codec_wiki SHIP cells. Expected outcome: bytes
around 35,000-40,000, SSIM2 around 85-87.

Methodology
-----------

Surgical single-knob change in `src/tuning.rs` ScreenVeryHigh tuple,
rebuild via `cargo build -p jxl-encoder --release --features
'__expert tuning-override parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop'
--example w44_phase4_s2_validate`, re-encode terminal e8 d=4 in
Mode B (opt-in path) with `EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl`, 8 threads, 8 GiB
budget. Each row also records the expanded `RuntimeTuning` values
(p3..p6) via a temporary debug `eprintln!` in the validate example
(removed before commit).

Per-cell measurement on terminal e8 d=4 in Mode B
-------------------------------------------------

See `w44_phase4_s2_refit_c1_ablation_2026-05-24.tsv`.

Headline rows:

| probe                | k1  | k2     | k3  | k4     | k5    | rt p3 | bytes | ssim2 | SHA256_8       |
|---                   |---  |---     |---  |---     |---    |---    |---    |---    |---             |
| baseline_default     | 0.5 | 1.0    | 1.0 | 3.5    | 0.0   | 4.000 | 42322 | 86.91 | 943d2b8b…      |
| s2_refit_raw         | 0.0 | 0.0    | 0.5 | 2.167  | -0.33 | ~0    | 28185 | 81.98 | 33c32773…      |
| c1_attempt_k2_0.333  | 0.0 | 0.333  | 0.5 | 2.167  | -0.33 | ~1.13 | 28185 | 81.98 | 33c32773…      |
| sweep_k2_0.5         | 0.0 | 0.5    | 0.5 | 2.167  | -0.33 | 2.542 | 28185 | 81.98 | 33c32773…      |
| sweep_k2_1.0         | 0.0 | 1.0    | 0.5 | 2.167  | -0.33 | 4.542 | 28185 | 81.98 | 33c32773…      |
| sweep_k2_1.5         | 0.0 | 1.5    | 0.5 | 2.167  | -0.33 | 5.942 | 28185 | 81.98 | 33c32773…      |
| isolated_k4_2.167    | 0.5 | 1.0    | 1.0 | 2.167  | 0.0   | 4.000 | 42322 | 86.91 | 943d2b8b…      |
| isolated_k3_0.5      | 0.5 | 1.0    | 0.5 | 3.5    | 0.0   | 4.000 | 42322 | 86.91 | 943d2b8b…      |
| **isolated_k1_0**    | 0.0 | 1.0    | 1.0 | 3.5    | 0.0   | 4.000 | **28185** | **81.98** | **33c32773…** |

**Three conclusions** the ablation forces:

1. **k2 is NOT the catastrophe driver.** Every value of k2 in {0, 0.333,
   0.5, 0.75, 1.0, 1.25, 1.5} (with other knobs at S2-refit values)
   produces BYTE-IDENTICAL output (SHA256 = 33c32773…) — even when
   `expand_to_runtime_tuning` returns rt.p3 = 5.94 (substantially above
   `DEFAULT_P3 = 4.0`). The W44-105 buttloop initial-seed scale is
   apparently overridden by the buttloop's own convergence: at e8 the
   loop iterates 4 times and the initial seed doesn't survive — the
   final qac field converges to whatever the discriminator + loop says
   is right.

2. **k4 and k3 alone are also not the catastrophe driver.** With true
   defaults everywhere except k4 = 2.167 (gate opens at d ≥ 2.167
   instead of 3.5), output is BYTE-IDENTICAL to baseline. Same with
   k3 = 0.5 (halved p5/p6). Both lower the screen-class lift, but at
   d = 4 the gate fires regardless, and neither change reaches the
   final qac field through the buttloop convergence.

3. **k1 = 0 ALONE reproduces the catastrophe.** With true defaults on
   every other knob, setting k1 = 0 (smoothness_bias = 0) produces
   BYTE-IDENTICAL output to the full S2-refit tuple — same SHA, same
   bytes, same SSIM2. This isolates k1 as the SOLE driver of the
   W44-228c1 violation on this cell.

Mechanism — k1 saturates p1 at ridge max
----------------------------------------

`k1 = smoothness_bias` feeds `p1 = smart_zenjxl_photo_mask_p25_min`
via the `p1_p2_smoothness_dispatch_ridge`:

   p1_unclamped = DEFAULT_P1 + (P1_RIDGE_MAX - DEFAULT_P1) * (1 - 2*s)

At s = 0.5 (default): p1 = DEFAULT_P1 = 85.0.
At s = 0     (k1=0):   p1 = P1_RIDGE_MAX (~145 per W44-218 ridge bounds).

`p1` is the threshold the W44-91/96/166 photo admit gates compare
mask1x1_p25 against — when p1 saturates at the ridge max, the gates
admit MORE images to the smart-zenjxl photo-class lift, which on
screen-class content disrupts the W44-105 screen-seed protection.

The c1 floor on k2 cannot close this because k2 only touches p3 and p6
(buttloop seed scale + e7 adaptive_quant lift), not p1 (the admit-gate
threshold).

Decision — HONEST-STOP
----------------------

Source REVERTED to S2-refit raw optima (k2 = 0 for screen/very_high).
The W44-105 SHIP-cell catastrophe on the opt-in path remains unfixed;
the W44-228c1 RULED-OUT default-flip constraint stays in force.

Acceptance gates per W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1 task spec:
  (a) screen/very_high k2 changed in src/tuning.rs                   N/A (reverted)
  (b) terminal e8 d=4 SSIM2 within 1.0 of 86.91 baseline             FAIL (81.98, delta -4.93)
  (c) 2 more W44-105 SHIP cells benched + verified protected         N/A (c1 mechanism doesn't work)
  (d) `cargo test --lib` PASS                                        PASS (1501/1501 after revert)
  (e) Strategy::Libjxl byte-lock + hash-lock all byte-identical      PASS (36/36 + 4/4)
  (f) Test `…aggressiveness_membership` updated                      N/A (kept original, k2 unchanged)
  (g) Documentation updated                                          PASS (in-source comment + this meta)
  (h) Drift test PASS                                                PASS (7/7)
  (i) Single commit pushed to main on origin                         (next step)
  (j) `.workongoing` removed                                         (next step)

Follow-on candidates (NOT in W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1 scope)
----------------------------------------------------------

A. **W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c2**: bisect a k1 floor on screen/very_high.
   Target: k1 ≥ 0.25 brings p1 within ±10 of `DEFAULT_P1 = 85`, the
   band the W44-105 chain was tuned against. Likely values to probe:
   {0.25, 0.333, 0.4, 0.5}. Must verify against terminal/imac_g3/
   codec_wiki e8+ d=4-6 + the gb82-sc spot-check cell on graph
   e8 d=5.0 (the OTHER big shifter S2-validate measured).

B. **W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c3**: per-stratum opt-in gates (e.g.,
   `LossyConfig::with_knobs_for_screen_low_only(true)`) so callers can
   harvest the screen/{mid,high} bytes wins without risking the
   screen/very_high catastrophe.

C. **Future Tier-2 sweep optimization criterion**: score per-stratum
   optima against bytes AND SSIM2 (Pareto), not bytes alone. The S1
   sweep's bytes-weighted criterion picked k1=0 because it minimizes
   bytes on the W44-PHASE4-S1 corpus (which did NOT contain the
   W44-105 SHIP cells). A Pareto criterion that weights SSIM2 cells
   like terminal e8 d=4 would have rejected k1=0.

DO NOT (future agents)
----------------------

1. DO NOT respawn W44-PHASE4-S2-refit-c1 expecting k2 to close this.
   Per-knob ablation is conclusive: k2 is structurally orthogonal to
   the catastrophe driver on this cell, even when expand returns
   rt.p3 above DEFAULT_P3.

2. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the -4.93 SSIM2 cliff. The
   ablation isolated k1 as the driver; this is a deliberate
   admit-gate threshold shift, not a numerical noise artifact.

3. DO NOT promote the W44-228c default-flip while screen/very_high's
   raw optimum carries k1=0. The W44-228c1 RULED-OUT memorandum
   (`benchmarks/w44_228c1_ship_cell_validation_2026-05-23.tsv`) plus
   this ablation are jointly load-bearing.

4. DO NOT change the membership test
   `w44_phase4_s2_refit_strata_aggressiveness_membership` without
   first verifying which knob actually drives the SHIP-cell SSIM2 on
   the cells the change would re-admit. k2 staying at 0 on
   screen/very_high is now a TRACKING pin, not a PROTECTION pin.

5. DO NOT re-launch sweep S2/S3 expecting different per-stratum k2
   values without first attacking the optimization-criterion bug
   (follow-on C above). The bytes-weighted criterion is structurally
   guaranteed to pick k1=0 + k2=0 on every screen stratum, even if
   that re-incurs the W44-105 catastrophe.

